{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent low bias: across all examples the model underpredicts the level by ~+2 to +7 EUR most of the time; apply an upward level shift, larger when the recent trend is up.",
    "Trend/lag error: the model reacts too slowly to strong upward momentum (it forecasts mild drift while realized prices step up); add a momentum term based on the last 5–10 day slope/returns, especially for horizons 1–15d.",
    "Horizon-dependent bias: underprediction is strongest in the front half (≈days 1–20). Use a larger positive correction early, tapering toward the back end of the 30d window.",
    "Over-mean-reversion after rallies: after a sharp rise the model pulls forecasts back down too quickly (often projecting declines to high-60s/low-70s while outcomes stay elevated); damp mean-reversion strength when 10–20d return is strongly positive.",
    "Peak/plateau miss: the model fails to capture sustained plateaus at new highs (upper-70s/low-80s), instead forecasting a rounded top; impose a regime rule—if price breaks above recent 20–30d high, keep forecasts near/above breakout level for ~1–2 weeks."
  ]
